Robert LeChevalier scripsit:

> >Is {da'a} by itself {da'apa} or {da'asu'o}? The latter is
> >indeed equivalent to {me'iro}.
> 
> It is elliptical in the same way that all of the other omitted words are 
> elliptical. 

Well, no. CLL 18.8 specifies that "da'a" by itself is "da'apa",
"all but one". Further, in ordinal contexts it means "all but the last".

